        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4f8061c3-3d66-5e96-979e-83732634ef6c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Centre for Medieval and Renaissance Studies, St. Olaf College\n- People: Michael Bauman, Bernt Julius Muus\n- Places: Oxford\n- Topics: American colleges and universities connected to CMRS\n\nFacts:\n- St. Olaf College was founded in 1874 by a group of Norwegian-American immigrant pastors and farmers led by Pastor Bernt Julius Muus.\n- The Centre for Medieval and Renaissance Studies in Oxford has received students from American colleges and universities including The University of Georgia, Elmhurst College, St. Mary's College of California, St. Mary's College of Maryland, St. Olaf College, William Jewell College, and Middlebury College.\n- Michael Bauman served for eight years as Lecturer and Tutor in Renaissance theology and literature at the Centre for Medieval and Renaissance Studies in Oxford.\n- Michael Bauman also served as Associate Dean of the Summer School at the Centre for Medieval and Renaissance Studies in Oxford.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a7149331-fa04-5d82-a038-b889fbb95122",
        "text": "Page: Centre for Medieval and Renaissance Studies. Sentence: Among the American colleges and universities that have sent students to CMRS are The University of Georgia, Elmhurst College, St. Mary's College of California, St. Mary's College of Maryland, St. Olaf College, William Jewell College, Middlebury College.\nPage: St. Olaf College. Sentence: It was founded in 1874 by a group of Norwegian-American immigrant pastors and farmers, led by Pastor Bernt Julius Muus.\nPage: Michael Bauman. Sentence: He was for eight years Lecturer and Tutor in Renaissance theology and Literature at the Centre for Medieval and Renaissance Studies, Oxford, where he also was Associate Dean of the Summer School.",
